<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truce of Yam-Zapolsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1582</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Truce of Yam-Zapolsky was signed on 15 January 1582 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, ending their part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-bathory">Stephen Báthory</a>'s campaigns and siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> gave up his conquests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a>, while Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> returned captured Russian border towns. The papal envoy Antonio Possevino mediated the talks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/truce-of-yam-zapolsky.jpg" alt="Truce of Yam-Zapolsky" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Matejko-Batory_pod_Pskowem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
